
                                               MEMMOVEACROSS COMMAND


Moves a range of data from source to destination address across files.

Below is the syntax :
 memMoveAcross 	-id ID1  -from fromAddress  -l len  -id2 ID2  -to toAddress  -o {"true"|"false"}  [-fill fillValue] 

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -id         |    ID value of the source hex file. ID value can be associated with a hex file using READ command.
   -from       |    Specifies source hex file address from where data has to be moved from. Mandatory switch.
   -l          |    Length of data to be moved. Mandatory switch.
   -id2        |    ID value of the destination hex file. ID value can be associated with a hex file using READ
               |    command.
   -to         |    Specifies destination hex file address at which data is written to. Mandatory switch.
   -o          |    Set overwrite either with true or false. Mandatory switch.
   -fill       |    Fills gaps with the one byte pattern provided. Optional switch.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	read -in input1.hex -igcks true ^
	memMoveAcross -id ID1 -from 0x80801000 -l 0x10 -id2 ID2 -to 0x80802000 -o true -fill 0xAA ^
	write -out outputFile.hex -lyt 0x10 ^
	exit
